WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:08.160
Did you know that if you have a property in Michigan
that you lost to tax foreclosure, it all may not be lost?

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.600
I need you to hear this.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:24.000
When a county takes title to your home or land, April 1st,
for a tax foreclosure, it turns around and has to sell
that property at public auction.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.960
And whoever buys it almost always pays more
than what you owed in taxes.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.040
That difference — that is called surplus.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.720
And it belongs to you, not the government.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.700
It's an obstacle course, though, to get the money back.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.880
You have to file forms, or require a notary.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.860
Eventually, a motion has to be filed in court.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:49.880
There's a hearing.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.120
It takes almost a year to get those funds.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:01:01.340
And that's all I do now — I work with people
so we can get the money back where it belongs.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:07.400
I would love to work with you, and get that money back in your hands.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.280
Please, feel free — call me.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.520
Text me, send an email, or fill out the form below.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:21.300
If you lost your Michigan property to a tax foreclosure,
so we can get that money back to you.
